where $\sigma_{\max}(X)$ denotes the maximum singular value of $X$. Finally, Lemma \ref{lem:extremesingularvalues} in Appendix \ref{app:aux} yields that $\sigma_{\max}(X) \leq \sqrt{2n} + \sqrt{d}$ with probability at least $1 - \exp(-c n)$, which concludes the proof.

